    "fields": {
      "question": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Calculate required control moment, elevator moment, and the change with airspeed. Explain whether the nominal response meets +0.12 rad/s²."
      },
      "system": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Illustrative planar pitch model. Aircraft geometry, integration, force conversion and constraints are supplied."
      },
      "representation": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Body axes forward/right/down. Positive pitch moment nose-up. Positive Fz downward. Positive elevator trailing edge down. Reference/CG X=0 m; tail X=-3 m."
      },
      "physics": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "Because if tail goes down nose goes up"
      },
      "assumptions": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "Planar motion, fixed reference, linear control effectiveness, and no trim/damping. These may fail with 3D motion, nonlinear control response, or significant trim/damping effects."
      },
      "inputs": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Iy=5000 kg·m²; target=+0.12 rad/s²; competing=-750 N-m; density=1.225 kg/m³; V=40 m/s; S=16 m²; chord=1.5 m; Cmδ=-0.8/rad; elevator=-5°. Inputs are illustrative, not calibrated."
      },
      "model": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "M_demand + M_competing = I_y × alpha_target\nDynamic pressure: q = 1/2 × rho × V²\nCoefficient: Delta Cm = Cm_delta_e × delta_e\nMoment: M = q × S × c × Delta Cm\nConvert: delta_e = delta_display × pi/180\n\nSupplied: rho, V, S, c, Cm_delta_e, I_y, alpha_target, M_competing.\nUnknown: delta_e."
      },
